ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Students get correct answers that cite the course page they come from"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "this is the change our classmates asked for" .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Every uploaded PDF becomes a valid graph of pages, chunks and topics"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "an answer can only be as good as the graph behind it" .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Students upload, ask and see answer quality from one web page"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "the prototype needed scripts run by hand for each new file" .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "No document, question or answer leaves the student's computer"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "course material belongs to the lecturers and must not go to outside services" .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The system lets a student upload course PDFs from a web page, extracts the text of every page, splits pages into chunks, computes an embedding for each chunk and stores documents, pages, chunks and topics in an RDF graph validated by SHACL shapes. For each question it selects candidate chunks with SPARQL by course and topic, ranks them by embedding similarity, sends the top three to a local LLM through Ollama and returns an answer with the document and page of each cited chunk. It records every answer with PROV-O. When no chunk is similar enough it says that the documents do not cover the question and gives no answer." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a lecture PDF that explains normalization is uploaded, when the student asks what third normal form is, then the answer cites the document and pages of the three chunks it used" .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given uploaded PDFs of a databases course, when the student asks about a topic none of them covers, then the assistant says no source was found and gives no answer" .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a scanned PDF with no text layer, when the student uploads it, then the file is refused and the message says it contains no text" .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Answers whose cited pages support the answer"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Judged ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of answers on the 50-question set where two team members agree the cited pages support the answer, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 (the prototype cites no page)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "85" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Recall@3 on the evaluation set"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of the 50 questions whose expected page is among the top 3 retrieved chunks, computed by the evaluation script" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "not measurable (the prototype returns only one chunk)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0.80" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Test PDFs that pass the shapes"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of the 20 test PDFs with a text layer whose graph passes pySHACL, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Steps from a new PDF to a cited answer"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "user actions needed to get an answer from a newly added PDF" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "4 (copy file, run embed.py, restart app, ask)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2 (upload, ask)" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O5 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Requests to outside services during a session"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "outgoing network connections other than to localhost logged during a full test run" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The student opens the page and uploads a PDF. The system extracts its text; if a page has no text the file is refused with a message. Otherwise it splits pages into chunks, computes embeddings, links chunks to topics and validates the graph with SHACL; on a violation the upload is rolled back and reported. The student chooses a course and asks a question. The retriever selects and ranks chunks; if none is similar enough the assistant says no source was found. Otherwise the LLM writes an answer from the top three chunks, citations are attached, the answer is recorded with PROV-O and shown." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The web page sends the question and course to the answer service. The answer service sends a SPARQL query to the graph store and receives the candidate chunks of that course. It asks the embedding model for the question vector, ranks the candidates and keeps the top three. It sends the question and the three chunks to Ollama and receives the draft answer. It writes a PROV-O record to the graph and returns the answer with document titles and page numbers to the web page, which shows each citation as a link to the page." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Document has a course code, a title, a file fingerprint and many Pages. Page has a page number and text and belongs to one Document. Chunk has text, an embedding and a position and belongs to one Page; a Chunk may discuss several Topics. Topic is a skos:Concept in the course's concept scheme. Question has a text and a chosen course. Answer has a text, a model name and many Citations, and is a prov:Entity generated from one Question. Citation links an Answer to one Chunk." .
